From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 14:00:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] virtiofs: the bulk data buffer is bound in the wrong
 direction

`vtfs_xfer()` binds the caller's bulk buffer with `DDI_DMA_WRITE`, but
that buffer is the device-writable tail of the chain: the device writes
the payload of a `FUSE_READ` or the dirent stream of a `FUSE_READDIR`
into it and we read it back.  `DDI_DMA_READ` is the direction that
says so.

Under QEMU on x86 this is harmless -- no bouncing happens and the
cookies name the same physical pages either way -- but the direction is
what an IOMMU is programmed from, and what `ddi_dma_sync(9F)` consults
on a platform where the two directions are not the same operation.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5)
---
 usr/src/uts/common/io/virtiofs/vtfs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/uts/common/io/virtiofs/vtfs.c b/usr/src/uts/common/io/virtiofs/vtfs.c
index a1af61b203..d0f57dd782 100644
--- a/usr/src/uts/common/io/virtiofs/vtfs.c
+++ b/usr/src/uts/common/io/virtiofs/vtfs.c
@@ -347,7 +347,7 @@ vtfs_xfer(vtfs_t *vtf, vtfs_xfer_t *vx)
 
 	if (vx->vx_data != NULL && vx->vx_datalen > 0) {
 		if (virtio_dma_bind(vs->vs_data, vx->vx_data, vx->vx_datalen,
-		    DDI_DMA_WRITE | DDI_DMA_STREAMING, KM_SLEEP) !=
+		    DDI_DMA_READ | DDI_DMA_STREAMING, KM_SLEEP) !=
 		    DDI_SUCCESS) {
 			r = ENOMEM;
 			goto out;
